COMMERCIAL S8.4 CANONICAL SERVER RE-ACCEPTANCE
Date: 2026-08-31

Goal
----
Bind the server to Application ef19c7b2a6d0b42cfe55e1e090878f72b29c64c2
(tree 250985b5464943b981a7654c39fa256ac7b695b4), apply migration 0024 exactly
once, validate the least-privilege contract, and conduct the authorized public
SFW re-acceptance while S7 remains healthy and available as fallback.

Preflight result
----------------
The Tailscale host identity, repository ownership, clean worktrees, S7 internal
and external health, PostgreSQL, resources, S8 inactive state, nginx, credential
metadata, and repository mutator boundaries were checked read-only. No unknown
Application/Control mutator or path collision was found. The server Application
and Control repositories are behind the authorized canonical targets, as
expected.

Risk
----
Migration 0024 changes durable PostgreSQL triggers and runtime grants. The
public activation changes only the already-approved S8 nginx target and starts
the bounded SFW service. S7 stays active. No adult media, AVS, payment, creator
activation, controlled beta, publishing, or production adult workflow is in
scope.

Backup and recovery gate
------------------------
Before migration 0024, create one fresh root-owned recovery point containing
verified Application/Control bundles, a custom-format database dump, a
schema-only dump, aggregate S8 counts, role/grant evidence, S8 configuration,
units, nginx state, credential metadata only, and SHA-256 verification. The S8
kill switch is the first rollback action. S8 and its timer are then stopped and
disabled; S7 remains live. Database restore is reserved for an independently
verified post-migration data or schema failure and must use the recorded dump.

Fail-closed boundaries
----------------------
Migration apply is rejected unless the 0023 state is exact and 0024 is either
fully absent or fully installed. Partial trigger/grant state is RED. Aggregate
business counts must be identical before and after apply. The runtime role must
not retain DELETE or TRUNCATE on notification deliveries and must pass the full
per-table privilege matrix. Any public hard failure closes S8 and preserves the
waitlist; no destructive data cleanup is permitted.

Initial status
--------------
AUTHORIZED_IN_PROGRESS

Public activation preflight correction
--------------------------------------
Before any public proxy change, the versioned activation helper was found to
still bind the superseded S8.3 Application commit/tree. Execution was stopped
before the helper ran. The helper is now bound to the S8.4 canonical
Application commit/tree recorded above, and the release-binding test covers
both the controller and public activation helper. No public or nginx mutation
occurred before this correction.

The subsequent public preflight also found the active proxy already matched
the exact versioned S8 candidate hash from the earlier reversible staging
attempt. The activation helper previously accepted only the exact S7 proxy
hash. It now accepts either of those two known hashes and continues to reject
